cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, data or report, please cite it as below."
title: "Routable historical road networks from old map sheets: a feasibility demonstration (historical-networks-prestudy)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexanderhellervik/historical-networks-prestudy"
authors:
  - family-names: Hellervik
    given-names: Alexander
    affiliation: Chalmers University of Technology
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5899-718X"
abstract: >-
  A pilot feasibility study for one corridor in western Sweden: routable road networks for the
  1890s (read from Häradsekonomiska kartan by AI models, reviewed and repaired), the 1960s
  (today's roads checked against Ekonomiska kartan) and today (OpenStreetMap), combined with
  parish population to give accessibility surfaces. Includes the pipeline code, the
  instructions given to the models, the shareable derived data, and a short report with effort,
  accuracy and scaling estimates. It is not a historical accessibility series and contains no
  analysis of population response.
keywords:
  - historical GIS
  - road networks
  - map digitisation
  - AI map reading
  - accessibility
  - Sweden
  - Häradsekonomiska kartan
  - Ekonomiska kartan
